{"query_id": "dp-long-chronicle", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "The Mill Lane chronicle records the following events concerning Greassby Mill in chronological order:\n\n1.  **1850**: The wheel at Greassby Mill turned again for the first time since the flood, watched by most of the street [5].\n2.  **1860-02-24**: Greassby Mill was sold by the estate to the miller's family, and the deed was witnessed at the inn [15].\n3.  **Post-gale repair**: The parish raised £4,525.32 by subscription to repair the roof of Greassby Mill after the gale [21].\n4.  **Mid-period maintenance**: Greassby Mill stood idle for 44 weeks while the millstones were re-dressed by a man brought in from the next county [19].\n5.  **Water flow reduction**: After the weir upstream was lowered, the leat at Greassby Mill carried only 17.5 per cent of its old flow [20].\n6.  **1887-12-21**: The last miller at Greassby Mill retired, and the building was let as a store [18].", "answer_sha256": "cea3250767fc565f10664a56176758fc79fd38112f4cc18afe7e6014e1ad774f", "ranked_ids": ["chronicle-long", "family-history-long"], "citation_map": {"1": "chronicle-long", "10": "chronicle-long", "11": "chronicle-long", "12": "chronicle-long", "13": "chronicle-long", "14": "chronicle-long", "15": "chronicle-long", "16": "chronicle-long", "17": "chronicle-long", "18": "chronicle-long", "19": "chronicle-long", "2": "chronicle-long", "20": "chronicle-long", "21": "chronicle-long", "22": "chronicle-long", "23": "chronicle-long", "24": "chronicle-long", "25": "chronicle-long", "26": "chronicle-long", "27": "family-history-long", "28": "chronicle-long", "3": "chronicle-long", "4": "chronicle-long", "5": "chronicle-long", "6": "chronicle-long", "7": "chronicle-long", "8": "chronicle-long", "9": "chronicle-long"}, "cited_ids": [5, 15, 21, 19, 20, 18], "cited_document_ids": ["chronicle-long"], "invalid_citations": [], "abstained": false, "expected_abstain": false, "mechanical_checks_passed"