{"query_id": "dp-long-choir-minutes", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "Based on the provided context, here are the records regarding the Holdmere fund found in the choir committee minutes and related documents:\n\n*   **Deposit for tour coach:** The deposit is due to Gearkwick Coaches by 2034-10-17; the balance is paid to the driver on the day of the tour [2].\n*   **Bank account closure:** The treasurer closed the old bank account of the Holdmere fund on 2029-09-22 and moved the balance to the building society [3].\n*   **Application deadline:** Applications to the Holdmere fund must be lodged 55 calendar days before the concert they are meant to support [4].\n*   **Spending limit:** It was resolved that no more than 65.5 per cent of the Holdmere fund may be spent in any one season [5].\n*   **Release for music stands:** £5,618.82 was released from the Holdmere fund towards new music stands [6].\n*   **Summer concert receipt:** The Holdmere fund received a further £6,133.78 from the retiring collection at the summer concert [7].\n*   **Next trustees' report:** The trustees of the Holdmere fund will next report to the committee on 2027-06-19 [8].\n*   **Reserve status (recurring note):** The treasurer noted that the reserve is healthy but should not be run down. This statement appears in the minutes for multiple meetings: Friday 1 September [10], Wednesday 16 May [11], Tuesday 9 January [12], Monday 13 August [16], Tuesday 23 September [17], Thursday 18 April [19], Tuesday 15 April [20], Tuesday 12 December [22], Monday 15 December [24], Wednesday 8 August [27] (attributed to Yusra Kellinghaus), and Monday 16 October [33].\n\n*   **Reserve status (Thursday 26 May):** According to Yusra Kellinghaus, the treasurer noted that the reserve is healthy but should not be run down [28].", "answer_sha256": "0230800dd4e2ae15ea48180a75f1a5d838c8a2b5c4ef43225542539cd5fb050c", "ranked_ids": ["choir-minutes-long", "note-coach-deposit", "policy