{"query_id": "dp-long-family-history", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "Based on the provided documents, here are the records established regarding Edith Fleastmere:\n\n*   **Baptism:** According to the baptism register in the family history notes, Edith Fleastmere was baptised on 1852-11-24 at the chapel on the hill [2].\n*   **Passenger details:** The passenger list indicates that Edith Fleastmere sailed on 1870-12-15, travelling alone and listed as a seamstress [5].\n*   **Journey duration:** Her letters state that the crossing took Edith Fleastmere 70 calendar days, most of it below deck [6].\n*   **Probate:** The probate record shows that Edith Fleastmere left £4,680.83, which was divided equally between her two daughters [3].\n*   **Burial:** The burial record states that Edith Fleastmere was buried on 1894-01-11, beside her husband in the lower churchyard [4].", "answer_sha256": "9af29a3cad57162261857972c14ab247049613843cfcb80ee237ae4fe6d181cf", "ranked_ids": ["family-history-long", "chronicle-long", "collision-dunlark-personal", "fragment-decoy-03"], "citation_map": {"1": "family-history-long", "10": "family-history-long", "11": "family-history-long", "12": "family-history-long", "13": "family-history-long", "14": "family-history-long", "15": "family-history-long", "16": "family-history-long", "17": "family-history-long", "18": "family-history-long", "19": "family-history-long", "2": "family-history-long", "20": "family-history-long", "21": "chronicle-long", "22": "chronicle-long", "23": "chronicle-long", "24": "chronicle-long", "25": "chronicle-long", "26": "chronicle-long", "27": "chronicle-long", "28": "collision-dunlark-personal", "29": "chronicle-long", "3": "family-history-long", "30": "fragment-decoy-03", "31": "chronicle-long", "4": "family-history-long", "5": "family-history-long", "6": "family-history-long", "7": "family-history-long", "8": "family-history-long", "9": "family-history-long"}, "cited_ids": [2, 5,